{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having some trouble with your left hand during dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. My hand gets so cold and hurts bad every time I go for dialysis. I can't even finish the session sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned you’ve been wearing a glove on your left hand?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:04:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it's always cold. Feels like it's never warm, even inside."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:05:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. This could be related to your AV fistula and something called steal syndrome. We saw your blood pressure was low in clinic—around 90s systolic—but you didn’t feel dizzy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I didn’t feel lightheaded or anything. Just weak sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’re going to hold off on your diltiazem and isosorbide for now. They might be lowering your blood pressure too much, which could worsen the blood flow to your hand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:08:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So those meds are making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-01-28 16:09:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll restart a lower dose once we stabilize things. Cardiology is reviewing your case to help manage your heart and blood pressure safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-01-29 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re going to do an arteriogram today to look at the blood flow in your left arm. It’s a special X-ray with contrast to see how blood moves through your arteries."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-01-29 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-01-29 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get some numbing medicine and light sedation. You might feel pressure, but not sharp pain. We need to see if there’s a blockage or why the blood isn’t reaching your hand well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-01-29 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got the results back from your arteriogram. Good news—no major blockages in the big arteries like the subclavian or brachial."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-01-29 17:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the cold and pain then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-01-29 17:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw poor filling in the smaller arteries—the radial and ulnar—down in your forearm. Even when we temporarily blocked the fistula and gave medicine to open the vessels, the flow didn’t improve much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-01-29 17:03:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the banding didn’t fix it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-01-29 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helped some, but not enough. The issue seems to be in the small vessels themselves. We don’t see a structural blockage, so it might be a circulation problem we can manage with medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-01-30 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re restarting your diltiazem at a lower dose—120 mg once daily. We’re also adding two new medications: digoxin and midodrine, which we’ll give before dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-01-30 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do those do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-01-30 08:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Digoxin helps your heart pump more efficiently. Midodrine helps raise your blood pressure during dialysis, so more blood can reach your hand and reduce steal symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-01-30 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I feel different?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-01-30 08:25:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so—less pain and coldness during dialysis. We’ll monitor your blood pressure closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-01-31 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned shoulder pain from a fall a few weeks ago. We’re going to get an X-ray of your left arm to check for any injury."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-01-31 10:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t think it was broken. Just hurts when I move it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-02-01 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray shows a healing fracture in the middle of your left humerus. It’s not displaced and is healing on its own. Ortho says no surgery needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-02-01 12:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A fracture? I didn’t know that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-02-01 12:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely from your fall. It’s stable and not near the joint, so it should heal with time. This might be contributing to your arm pain, separate from the fistula issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-02-01 12:04:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the pain isn’t all from the dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-02-01 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. The fracture explains the shoulder and upper arm pain. The coldness and pain during dialysis are still from the steal syndrome, but we’re treating that differently now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How did dialysis go this morning? Any pain or coldness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I didn’t have to stop early. The pain was less, and my hand wasn’t as cold."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. The midodrine and digoxin seem to be helping. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need to take these meds forever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with digoxin every other day and midodrine before each dialysis. We need to check your digoxin level in a few days to make sure it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-02-02 13:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only if the level gets too high. We’ll monitor it closely. The goal is 0.6 to 1.2. As long as it’s in range, it’s safe and helps your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today to an extended care facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Am I fixed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not completely, but we’ve improved things. Your hand pain during dialysis is better, and your blood pressure is more stable. The fracture will heal on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do I need to watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor if your left hand gets colder, more painful, turns blue, or you lose grip strength. Also check your fistula daily for the buzzing sound and pulse—called bruit and thrill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if I don’t feel it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call right away. That could mean the fistula is clotting. Don’t wait for your dialysis day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue most as before. Diltiazem is now 120 mg daily, digoxin every other day, and midodrine before dialysis. Keep taking your insulin, gabapentin, and other usual meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:11:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before—low sodium, low potassium, low phosphorus. Follow your nephrologist’s fluid limits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure your records go to the facility. Keep up with your dialysis and follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care, and call if anything changes with your hand or fistula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your nephrologist will follow up. We’ll coordinate care. Just focus on healing and staying on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're doing great. We’ll get you discharged shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep wearing that glove if it helps. It’s okay to protect your hand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Feels better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. We’re making progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re a team. You’re doing your part—staying engaged and asking questions. That helps us help you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you will. We’ve got a plan, and you’re responding well. Keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Rest up, and the care team will get you ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2151-02-03 08:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll be in touch if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-01-28 16:01:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-02-03 13:22:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis was admitted due to persistent steal syndrome symptoms in his left hand despite prior fistula banding. He reported chronic coldness and severe pain during dialysis, requiring early session termination. Hypotension was noted, prompting temporary hold of diltiazem and isosorbide. After cardiology consultation, he was restarted on a lower dose of diltiazem and initiated on digoxin and midodrine before dialysis, which improved blood pressure and reduced steal symptoms. An arteriogram showed no major arterial blockages but persistent poor distal radial and ulnar artery filling, even after fistula compression and nitroglycerin. A healing, non-displaced mid-humerus fracture was incidentally found on X-ray, contributing to shoulder pain. He responded well to treatment, completed dialysis without pain, and was discharged to an extended care facility with medication adjustments, fistula monitoring instructions, and plans for digoxin level checks.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Closed fracture of shaft of humerus",
      "Other specified procedures as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified viral hepatitis C without hepatic coma",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Gout, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Cocaine abuse, unspecified",
      "Fracture, cause unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
